  "note": "Official Qwen3.8-27B-FP8 on ONE B70 (32 GiB), R312d-c image: host-memory input embedding, MTP depth 5 with the draft-only INT4 shortlist head, the single-checkpoint recurrent state (one GDN state block per request, replay-commit of the accepted prefix) and the one-pass verifier attention (the draft's 2-6 rows computed in a single pass over the cache instead of one pass each), 32,768-token context at 0.975 memory. The first server is the September 18 lc-4 campaign (research launcher); the second is the September 18 acceptance campaign through the package launcher, which also repeated the suite on the same server at 54.011. Both servers are 12/12 identical to the same-image no-MTP server at the 896-token attention block (itself 12/12 identical to the 832-token no-MTP reference); the package server is also 64/64 on the 64-prompt sequential oracle plus two queued passes, exact on the 2K/8K/16K context screen, the 2,048-30,720-token long corpus in three content types, the chat quality suite and the 21-request logprob replay, and stopped cleanly. Outputs are byte-identical to the R311b record this supersedes (cmu5wc2e50804lq01r0br2i5p); the change is speed after long prompts (+9.9% at 16K, +14.5% at 24K, +17.3% at 30K) at the same short-prompt headline."
